        <body>
            <div type="edition" xml:id="edition-text">
                <div type="textpart" subtype="book" n="19" xml:id="problem6">
                    <div type="textpart" subtype="problem" n="6">
                      <div type="section">
                        <head>Expositio problematum Aristotelis, Particula XIX: De harmonia</head>
                         <head>By Pietro d'Abano, edited by Caleb Mutch</head> 
                          <p n="1">
                              This is a sample of my critical edition of Pietro d'Abano's commentary on book XIX 
                              ("Concerning Music") of the pseudo-Aristotelian Problemata. The Problemata was the 
                              first Ancient Greek text discussing music in detail to be rediscovered in the High 
                              Medieval period, and it contains much information about musical performance practice
                              that would have been unfamiliar to readers at the time, for whom Boethius's speculative
                              approach to music theorizing was authoritative. Consequently, the unfamiliar material
                              was in need of a commentator.
                          </p>
                          <p n="2">
                              Pietro d'Abano, an Italian polymath who lived about the turn of the fourteenth century,
                              set himself the task of explaining the entirety of the Problemata, a thirty-nine-book
                              tome that seeks to explain much of the natural world. The specific text he commented on
                              was a recently completed Latin translation that followed the usual practice of rendering
                              each Greke word with its closest Latin equivalent, rendering an entirely unidiomatic Latin
                              text. Consequently, Pietro first paraphrases the text into a more Latinate version, and 
                              then he explains the issues that arise. 
                          </p>
                          <p n="3">
                              My XML encoding of the text classifies every textual variant, allowing for readers to filter 
                              out types of variation (differences in spelling, word ordering, and so forth) as they like.
                              Variants may be viewed by mousing-over the dialog boxes beside each paragraph of the text,
                              or viewed in the traditional Apparatus Criticus format below. Clicking on the dialog boxes
                              allows viewers to substitute their chosen variants into the main text. The abbreviations
                              following each reading indicate which manuscript or family of manuscripts contains that
                              reading; an account of all the manuscripts (including hyperlinks to online versions, where
                              available) may be found at the end of the page. 
                          </p>
                          <p n="4">
                              I have also enabled readers to filter out readings found only in Jean de Jandun's
                              redaction of the text. Shortly after Pietro finished his commentary, Jean (a leading 
                              scholar at the University of Paris) produced a revision of Pietro's work, and a third of
                              the surviving manuscripts descend from Jean's redaction. As a result, they do not help
                              to establish Pietro's original text, but they provide an informative witness to the text's
                              reception at a major source of learning. My thanks to the <ref 
                              target="https://digitallatin.org/">Digital Latin Library</ref>, from whom I have adapted 
                              this "reading room" viewer for XML-based critical editions.
                          </p>
                      </div>
                      <div type="section">
                        <head><num type="ordinal" value="6">Sextum</num> problema</head>
                        <p n="1"><mentioned><seg xml:id="ment-6.1" n="1">PROPTER QUID PAR YPATE SECUNDUM
                            RATIONEM IN CANTIBUS TRAGICUM.</seg>
                            <seg xml:id="ment-6.2" n="2">AUT PROPTER INEQUALITATEM? PASSIUUM ENIM INEQUALE, 
                                ET IN MAGNITUDINE FORTUNE AUT TRISTITIE. EQUALE AUTEM MINUS PLORABILE UEL 
                                ULULABILE.</seg></mentioned>
                            <gloss target="#ment-6.1"><app>
                                <lem>Quare</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#λ" ana="#additive">Querit quare</rdg>
                            </app> rationabile <app>
                                <lem>existit</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π" ana="#lexical #J">est</rdg>
                            </app> quod genus <app>
                                <lem>cantandi</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π" ana="#subtractive #J"/>
                            </app> tragicum per ypatem cantetur?</gloss>
                            Nosce <app>
                                <lem>quod</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π #Ma" ana="#subtractive"/>
                            </app> circa genus armonicum quodcumque duplicem maneriem cantandi 
                            constare, quedam enim est <app>
                                <lem>comedia</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π" ana="#additive #J">comedia et</rdg>
                            </app> altera tragedia. Est autem comedia canticum agreste <app>
                                <lem>que</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π" ana="#subtractive #J"/>
                            </app> res priuatarum et humilium personarum
                            <app>
                                <lem>comprehendit</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π" ana="#morphological #J">comprehendens</rdg>
                            </app>, et dicitur a cosmos quod est villa <app>
                                <lem>vel laus</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π #Ea" ana="#subtractive"/>
                            </app> secundum aliquos. 
                            Grece tamen mundus et odi cantus quasi mundanus et vulgaris cantus, de rebus enim 
                            vulgaribus tractat et affinibus cotidiane <app>
                                <lem>locutionis</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π #Ea #Nu #Va" ana="#morphological">locutioni</rdg>
                            </app>. Vel dicitur <app>
                                <lem>a commessatione</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π" ana="#additive #J">a commessatione quia</rdg>
                                <rdg wit="#Ea #Nu" ana="#lexical">accessatione</rdg>
                            </app> post cibum, <app>
                                <lem>enim</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π" ana="#subtractive #J"/>
                            </app> homines solebant ad eam audiendam conuenire. Tragedia vero est modus carminis 
                            quo poete in luctibus regum vtebantur. <app>
                                <lem>Dicta</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π" ana="#morphological #J">Dictus</rdg>
                            </app> a tragos quod <app>
                                <lem>est</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#Ma #Px #Vm" ana="#lexical">dicitur</rdg>
                            </app> yrcus et odi cantus <app>
                                <lem>quasi</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#β #Ea #Vb #Vo" ana="#lexical">inde</rdg>
                            </app> hyrcinus cantus. Et quia materia erat <app>
                                <lem>tristis</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#λ" ana="#additive">tristis et</rdg>
                            </app>
                            <app>
                                <lem>feda</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#β #γ #Ma #Px" ana="#lexical">seda</rdg>
                            </app>, <app>
                                <lem>huiusmodi</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#κ #Ea #Va #Vo" ana="#lexical">huius</rdg>
                            </app> animal vt yrcum pro munere <app>
                                <lem>poematis</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π" ana="#subtractive #J"/>
                            </app> accipiebant additur. <app>
                                <lem>Et</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π #Nu" ana="#lexical">Etiam</rdg>
                            </app>
                            maneries a <app>
                                <lem>quibus</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#π #Ma #Nu" ana="#lexical">quibusdam</rdg>
                            </app> <num type="ordinal" value="3">3°</num> satira dicta que carmine <app>
                                <lem>construitur</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#γ" ana="#lexical">constituitur</rdg>
                            </app> reprehensorio ceu modus 
                            <persName ref="http://viaf.org/viaf/100227522">oratii</persName>
                                fuit maxime.</p>
                          <p n="2"><app>
                              <lem n="maxime"/>
                              <rdg wit="#Va #m #v" ana="#additive">Deinde.</rdg>
                          </app>
                              <mentioned><ref target="#ment-6.2">AUT.</ref></mentioned> 
                              Soluit dicens causam esse sumptam
                              <gloss target="#ment-6.2">ab inequalitate, vtrobique <app>
                                  <lem>enim</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#β #γ" ana="#lexical">videlicet</rdg>
                              </app> inest quedam inequalitas</gloss>, 
                              vt in cantu tragico et <app>
                                  <lem>per ypatem</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#Ma #Pu #Pz" ana="#lexical">parypaten</rdg>
                              </app> facto, propter <app>
                                  <lem>eius</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#π" ana="#morphological #J">eam</rdg>
                              </app> esse
                              <app>
                                  <lem>supremum</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#π" ana="#morphological #J">supremam</rdg>
                              </app>. Nam in vnoquoque istorum est quedam passio et difficultas, quod autem <app>
                                  <lem>tale</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#λ" ana="#additive">tale est</rdg>
                              </app>, <app>
                                  <lem>siue</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#Vo" ana="#lexical #J">seu</rdg>
                                  <rdg wit="#Gu #Pq" ana="#additive #J">Inequale seu</rdg>
                              </app> sit 
                              <gloss target="#ment-6.2">in magnitudine <app>
                                  <lem>
                                      <app>
                                          <lem>fortune</lem>
                                          <rdg wit="#γ #Px #Vm #Vz" ana="#lexical">fortitudine</rdg>
                                      </app> ceu cantus magne letitie alicuius <app>
                                          <lem>magnatis</lem>
                                          <rdg wit="#γ #Nu" ana="#additive">magnatis et</rdg>
                                      </app> probitatis, siue in magnitudine</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#π #Ea" cause="homeoteleuton" ana="#subtractive"/>
                              </app> tristitie</gloss>, sicut mortis alicuius excellentis <app>
                                  <lem>vel</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#π #Ea #Py" ana="#subtractive"/>
                              </app>
                              <app>
                                  <lem>huiusmodi</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#κ #Ea #Nu #Va #Vo" ana="#lexical">huius</rdg>
                              </app>, est inequale, non eundem seruans tenorem. Quod autem est inequale et dissonum <app>
                                  <lem>rationabile</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#Vm #Vz" ana="#morphological">rationale</rdg>
                              </app> est, vt cantu exprimatur <app>
                                  <lem>huiusmodi</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#κ #Ea #Vo" ana="#lexical">huius</rdg>
                              </app>, vt pondus meloticum configeretur rei de qua existit. 
                              Tunc cantus consurgit <cit>
                                <quote rend="inline" xml:id="quote-6.1-Gal">"eurithimus"</quote>
                                  <ref>sicut de <app>
                                      <lem>huius</lem>
                                      <rdg wit="#Nu #Vb" ana="#lexical">huiusmodi</rdg>
                                  </app> pulsu scribitur 
                                <ref><title ref="https://viaf.org/viaf/2531163877720046060000/">de
                                    differentiis pulsuum</title></ref>
                                    <bibl><seg>a</seg></bibl>
                                      <name ref="https://viaf.org/viaf/44299175/">galeno.</name></ref>
                              </cit> <app>
                                  <lem>Ceu</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#Ea #Vo" ana="#lexical">Seu</rdg>
                              </app> in bellis tubarum clangor bellantes concitat in furorem, 
                              in oppositis autem vt in choreis oppositum <app>
                                  <lem>expetitur</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#γ #Vo" ana="#lexical">experitur</rdg>
                              </app>, ac similiter in mortuorum lamentatione. Et <app>
                                  <lem>id</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#α" ana="#lexical">illud</rdg>
                                  <rdg wit="#π" ana="#lexical #J">hoc</rdg>
                              </app> est quod <app>
                                  <lem>subditur</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#π #Ea" ana="#morphological">subdit</rdg>
                              </app> a contrariis probando pretactum, inquiens quod <gloss target="#ment-6.2">
                                  illud quod est equale in cantu et vnum conseruans tenorem non est <app>
                                      <lem>plorabile</lem>
                                      <rdg wit="#γ" ana="#lexical">proportionabile</rdg>
                                  </app> aut <app>
                                      <lem>ululabile</lem>
                                      <rdg wit="#π" ana="#lexical #J">lamentabile</rdg>
                                  </app></gloss>, 
                              cum non sit quid passiuum, propter quod non est conueniens ipsum <app>
                                  <lem>parypatem</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#β #γ #Vz" ana="#lexical">per ypatem</rdg>
                              </app> cuius est inequalitatem tenere sed per alias <app>
                                  <lem>cordarum</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#π #Px #Vb" ana="#morphological">cordas</rdg>
                              </app>
                              <app>
                                  <lem>mitiores</lem>
                                  <rdg wit="#Gu #Pp #Pu" ana="#lexical #J">anteriores</rdg>
                              </app> exponere.</p>
                        <p n="3">Nosce quod <cit>
                                <quote rend="inline">"pondus est illud in <app>
                                        <lem>quo</lem>
                                        <rdg wit="#Ca #Pu #Vo" ana="#morphological #J">quod</rdg>
                                        <rdg wit="#Pp #Pq #Pz" ana="#morphological #J">quid</rdg>
                                    </app> proportiones"</quote>
                                <app>
                                    <lem>secundum 
                                      <persName ref="http://viaf.org/viaf/89770781">auicenna</persName></lem>
                                    <rdg wit="#π" ana="#subtractive #J"/>
                                </app>
                                <quote rend="inline">
                                    "<app>
                                        <lem>cadunt musice</lem>
                                        <rdg wit="#π" ana="#ordinal #J">musice cadunt</rdg>
                                    </app>."</quote>
                        </cit> Hoc autem pondus <app>
                            <lem>rebus expedit</lem>
                            <rdg wit="#π" ana="#additive #J">expedit conformari rebus</rdg>
                        </app> circa quas extat <app>
                            <lem>configurari</lem>
                            <rdg wit="#π" ana="#subtractive #J"/>
                        </app>, cum eo exprimantur passiones que sunt in anima. <cit>
                                <quote rend="inline">
                                    "Voces enim sunt  note passionum que sunt in <app>
                                        <lem>ea</lem>
                                        <rdg wit="#Gu #Pp #Pu" ana="#lexical #J">anima</rdg>
                                    </app>
                                    illeque rerum"</quote>
                                <bibl><biblScope unit="book" n="1"><num type="ordinal"
                                      value="1">primo</num></biblScope></bibl>
                                    <ref><title ref="http://viaf.org/viaf/186598616">peryarmenias.</title>
                                    </ref></cit> 
                            Vnde si res fuerit <app>
                                <lem>alta</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#Pp #Pq #Pu" ana="#lexical">altera</rdg>
                            </app> in signis <app>
                                <lem>contingit</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#Ma #Nu #Pz" ana="#lexical">conuenit</rdg>
                            </app> tragedia ipsam exprimere. 
                            Si autem econtra comedia vt modus coaptetur rei <app>
                                <lem>ceu</lem>
                                <rdg wit="#Ea #Vm #Vo" ana="#lexical">seu</rdg>
                            </app> proprietas subiecto.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
            </div>
